="f415b362-1c56-478c-8b2a-95f977f572d6" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="creapure" tabindex="-1" id="creapure" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-1sazcsn"><div data-rid="b1173d2b-9623-4762-a188-0f93d9c18f9a" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-twyijh"><div data-rid="c21702f3-967a-4d49-84b6-0c5e964b271c" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1gwwcfz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>1. Creatine gives you more energy throughout your day.</p></span></div><div data-rid="8f4b4333-d661-4639-b38d-a51ee2a30b0c" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-155i2az alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Creatine's core function is increasing the production of ATP, the most basic form of energy in your body's cells. ATP plays a crucial role in metabolism and muscular function in particular.</p><p><br></p><p>Whether you're looking to stay focused throughout your workday, aiming to hit that next level in a workout, or you need more energy to enjoy time with friends and family, creatine can support you across all of your goals.</p><br><p>Create's Daily Performance Gummies further supplement the impact of creatine with a nootropic gummy blend.</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="83fd6f4c-9c2d-459c-8def-16e4e1127a0e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1uc8cvh"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_GreenBG-min.webp?v=1739201540&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_GreenBG-min.webp?v=1739201540&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_GreenBG-min.webp?v=1739201540&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_GreenBG-min.webp?v=1739201540" alt="Explanation of how creatine aids ATP recovery for energy." class="r-1nfc3h1" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="f63ee860-3b3a-43ed-b5ec-9f2f4b8d8e5c" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" class="r-46y8qm"><div data-rid="5e6c9e0a-35a8-4dd8-a41b-766c83a082be" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-s3o9se"><div data-rid="f8b21622-d3df-4b8b-bc39-32e26e9fb52b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-6odqwy"><div class="r-7jrszq"><video style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:var(--rof, inherit);object-position:var(--rop, inherit)" preload="metadata" autoplay="" muted="" loop=""></video></div></div></div><div data-rid="627432f7-6b01-4413-b1a4-82d30e1dfe15" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1ghyfjc"><div data-rid="a279ec3a-2159-4cb3-89a8-40687d7ffc78" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-wdd5yr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>2. Proper supplementation can help increase strength without bulk.</p></span></div><div data-rid="37295464-96f5-437e-9199-a843f9467f94" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-przo01 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>One of the most common misconceptions around creatine is that it's used solely by bodybuilders looking to get huge. In fact, creatine is highly associated with the development of lean muscle. </p><br><p>Creatine also facilitates exercises associated with building lean, toned muscle like high-energy interval training (HIIT) and endurance sports, along with the more traditional weightlifting efforts.</p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="913e4cd9-5503-4919-a979-f13abf813c05" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="influencers" tabindex="-1" id="influencers" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-hrshzg"><div data-rid="5b21f05d-e40b-4d59-a625-1891b936d659" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1b8c42g"><div data-rid="bfe69f29-75df-4760-a2a3-38458bd30772" data